/-!
# Very tame quotients of log regular pairs

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Exposé VI, Theorem 3.2 and Proposition 3.5(c),
printed pp. 73--76; VI 1.4 and IX 2.4 for the pair formulation
(blueprint: lem-per-very-tame-quotient-log-regular).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The invariant direct image of the divisorial log structure under an admissible,
generically free, very tame finite group quotient is fs log regular. The section
equivalences commute with the structural maps to regular functions, identifying the
log structure with the actual invariant direct image. Its triviality locus is the
complement of the image of the boundary, and this gives a log regular quotient pair.

Source: ILO VI 3.2, 3.5(c), 3.7(a)--(c), VI 1.4 and IX 2.4
(blueprint: lem-per-very-tame-quotient-log-regular).

Proof:
1. Put N = (q_* M_D)^G. Its structural map lands in the invariant functions O_Y;
an invariant section mapping to a unit has invariant inverse, so N is a log structure.
By lem-per-finite-quotient-strict-local-invariants, Y is Noetherian and, at a
geometric point and a lift, B = A^H, A is finite over B and N_y = M_x^H. The
geometric fibres are orbits, and H is the geometric stabilizer.
2. The log regular pair supplies fs charts, a regular stratum A/I and the dimension
formula. Very tameness gives invertible |H| and trivial actions on the characteristic
and stratum. By lem-per-very-tame-equivariant-sharp-chart choose a sharp equivariant
chart Q with diagonal character; I is generated by its nonidentity monomials.
3. Apply lem-per-very-tame-local-kummer-quotient: the invariant chart P is the
intersection of Q with the common character kernel L, is fs sharp, and P^gp = L
contains |H| Q^gp. Its stratum quotient B/J is A/I. The strict-local comparison
identifies this chart with N, and its neighbourhood clause supplies étale-local
charts on Y, proving fine saturation.
4. By lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral and
lem-weil-pbc-integral-injective-dimension-equal, dim B = dim A. The finite-index
inclusion L in Q^gp gives equal rational ranks. Substituting B/J = A/I gives
the log dimension formula for B, and B/J is regular. Thus N is log regular.
5. The finite-index sharp saturated charts give P trivial iff Q is trivial:
if P is trivial, a positive multiple of every q is zero; saturation and sharpness
make Q^gp torsion free. Hence triviality is equivalent at each geometric point and
its lift. The boundary is invariant and fibres are orbits, so the triviality locus
is Y minus q(E). By lem-trf-log-regular-divisorial-structure it is open dense and
N is its divisorial log structure, giving the asserted log regular pair.
-/
theorem veryTame_quotient_logRegular
    {D Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral D] [IsNoetherian D]
    (U : D.Opens) (hU : DenseRange U.ι)
    (hpair : IsDivisorialFineSaturatedLogRegularPair D U.toScheme U.ι hU)
    {G : Type v} [Group G] [Finite G] (a : G →* Aut D)
    (hpres : ∀ (g : G) (x : D), (a g).hom x ∈ U ↔ x ∈ U)
    (hfree : ∃ V : D.Opens, Dense (V : Set D) ∧
      (∀ (g : G) (x : D), (a g).hom x ∈ V ↔ x ∈ V) ∧
      ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω]
        (t : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ D) (g : G),
        t default ∈ V → t ≫ (a g).hom = t → g = 1)
    (htame : IsVeryTameDivisorialAction U a)
    (q : D ⟶ Y) (hq : IsAdmissibleFiniteSchemeQuotient a q) :
    ∃ (hY : IsLocallyNoetherian Y) (N : EtaleLogStructure Y)
      (e : ∀ W : Y.Etale, N.monoidSheaf.obj.obj (op W) ≃*
        invariantDivisorialDirectImageSections U a q hq.2.2.1 W),
      (∀ (W : Y.Etale) (s : N.monoidSheaf.obj.obj (op W)),
        (pullback.fst W.hom q).appTop (N.alpha.app (op W) s) = (e W s).val) ∧
      ∃ hfs : N.IsFineSaturated,
        FineSaturatedLogScheme.IsLogRegular ⟨Y, hY, N, hfs⟩ ∧
        N.trivialityLocus = (q '' (U : Set D)ᶜ)ᶜ ∧
        ∃ (V : Y.Opens) (hV : DenseRange V.ι),
          (V : Set Y) = (q '' (U : Set D)ᶜ)ᶜ ∧
          @IsDivisorialFineSaturatedLogRegularPair Y V.toScheme V.ι
            inferInstance hY hV := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
